---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
---
<Base
  title="Wrong Cable | Save My Gig"
  description="This page doesn't exist. But your gig can still be saved."
  path="/404"
  noindex
>
  {/* ONE ALIGNMENT AXIS (2026-08-06). The eyebrow carried
      justify-content:center and the CTA carried margin:0 auto, so at 1280 this
      page centred two of its five elements while the h1, the paragraph and the
      Home link sat on the left column every other page on the site uses. Two
      axes on one screen reads as a page assembled from two templates, and this
      is a crisis surface: a reader arriving here is already confused about
      where they are.
      /offline is the reference and it is not an arbitrary one: it is the other
      crisis surface, it carries the same red route out, and it has always been
      left-aligned with a plain full-width .btn. So the inline styles are
      DELETED rather than adjusted, and the two pages now differ in copy only.
      The pt and es copies name this file as their structural source, so the
      reasoning is not repeated in them. */}
  <main class="wrap" style="padding-top:4rem">
    <div class="status-line red">Signal_Lost</div>
    <h1 class="danger" style="margin-bottom:1rem">404 - WRONG CABLE</h1>
    <p class="dim" style="margin-bottom:2rem">This page isn't plugged in. But if your USB just died before a gig, you're two taps from the fix.</p>
    <a href="/emergency" class="btn btn-solid"><Icon name="siren" /> Start Emergency Mode</a>
    <p style="margin-top:1.5rem"><a href="/" class="dim" style="text-decoration:none">← Home</a></p>
  </main>
</Base>
